 ## 6. Placement of judgment
 
 - **REQ-28** Deterministic Go owns eligibility, cache keys, identity, gate, measurements, trend flags, redaction; Jev ranks/routes **on from launch** and only annotates (output is an `annotation` row; `issues` does not import `decisions`); reasoning LLMs are opt-in discovery; humans own dispositions, policy, activation (design §6, Appendix 4).
 - **REQ-29** Jev guardrails: typed `noul|choice|score` questions with `question_id@<sha256 version key over instructions, criteria, state shape, question kind, option-order rule, resolved model>`; rank-formula and baseline versions stored with every ranking and disposition; resolved-model pinning (mismatch → discarded, unit `incomplete`); cap `policy.decisions.max_per_run` (default 2,000) and billed-cost cap `policy.decisions.max_cost_usd` (default $0.50 **[ASSUMPTION]**; the run stops when billed cost is unreported); unranked view always available; nightly audit is a probability sample with a stored inclusion probability per unit, presented blind (annotation, stratum and rank hidden); the interim draw is independent per unit at that probability under a stored audit-sampler version, with a provisional 5 % total until X1's preregistration is signed off (sampling unit, strata, draws and floor fixed there) and Jev-quality lines `insufficient` until then; every disposition records its view (audit or not) and annotation visibility; deterministic ranking baseline used and disclosed on fork PRs or without key/egress, and stored for every finding so X1 can measure Jev's gain; launch pin `typesafe/jev-1.14-20261014` via OpenRouter `alpha/decisions` (dated slug only; undated release lines and aliases rejected), status `provisional` with per-finding disclosure, per-decision minimums defaulting to 0.8/0.8 raised to 0.9 on the costlier side until the user sets them (tuning minimums for `triage.real_defect`, gating nothing while ranking is ordinal; the defaults substitute only for precision/recall point minimums (X3, X10, point values in X5); X1's gain threshold and the lower-bound forms (X4, X5) have no default substitute; the X1/X3/X4/X5/X10 values stay rev 2.1 values until their preregistrations confirm or replace them); the adapter follows the practices `docs/jev-adapter-audit.md` records as Met or Fixed (Design-level rows 5, 35, 38 remain open; backlog B-1–B-4 records the follow-ups, B-3 running the row-30 flip-rate harness on the first Choice that gates anything) (design §6, §13 X1, Appendix 19).
 - **REQ-30** Jev never closes or dismisses issues, never defines identity, and `P(real_defect)` is not presented as calibrated confidence (design §6 "Rejected"; E2 `evaluation/jev-triage-v1/RESULTS.md`).
